Program 1: Tar Archiver
CS3411 Spring 2025

This program did not require a README, so I'm making one now for Github.

The main goal of this program was to create a function (stored in f.c) which when called by
another function can predictably store and retrieve data in pointers without resulting in any 
memory leaks. It is operated by commands, which are typed as integers but are references by the
macros in both files:
    F_first (1) and F_last (2) allocate and free the associated memory, respectively
    F_data_int (3), F_data_char (4) and F_data_float (5) each store their associated type
    F_print (6) prints all of the stored data

